config PKVM_S2MPU
	tristate "S2MPU driver compatible with pKVM"
	default n
	help
	This module is a driver for the stage-2 IOMMU controlled by hypervisor.

config PKVM_S2MPU_V9
	tristate "S2MPU V9 driver compatible with pKVM"
	default n
	help
	This module is a driver for the stage-2 IOMMU controlled by hypervisor.

config S2MPU_BYPASS
	tristate "S2MPU driver of bypass mode"
	default n
	depends on !PKVM_S2MPU && !PKVM_S2MPU_V9
	help
	  This option enables a minimal S2MPU driver that puts the S2MPU
	  (Stage 2 Memory Protection Unit) into bypass mode.

	  When the S2MPU comes out of reset, it blocks all DMA traffic,
	  preventing devices from accessing the memory system. This minimal
	  driver initializes the S2MPU to a bypass mode, allowing devices
	  to function.

	  The primary purpose of this driver is to facilitate early kernel
	  bring-up during in-market kernel upgrades. The full S2MPU
	  driver has a dependency on the pKVM IOMMU framework, which can
	  undergo significant changes between kernel versions, making it
	  challenging to integrate during upgrades.

	  This minimal driver, in contrast, uses stable Linux kernel APIs
	  that are less likely to change, ensuring forward compatibility.
	  It is intended to be used until the pKVM IOMMU framework in a
	  given Android LTS kernel is stable.

	  If you are not performing an in-market kernel upgrade or require
	  the full functionality of the pKVM IOMMU, you should say N here.

config KERNEL_TOP
	tristate "Display processes statistic"
	default n
	help
	  This module exposes kernel function for modules to debugging
	  processes statistic.

config GOOGLE_MODEMCTL
	tristate "Common modem control interfaces"
